# 28. The pitch

Your opening could be:

> **Healthcare doesn't have a knowledge problem. It has a journey problem.**
>
> Patients receive PDFs, instructions, forms, emails and phone calls, but they still don't know what they should do next.
>
> CarePath AI turns a clinic's existing protocols and documents into a personalized AI-guided care journey.
>
> Clinics upload their protocols. AI builds the journey. Patients get an intelligent guide that understands where they are, what they've completed, and what comes next.
>
> And unlike a traditional workflow system, CarePath learns where patients are getting stuck and helps the clinic improve the journey.

### The killer line:

> **"We don't give patients another portal. We give them an AI that knows their journey."**

That is the direction I'd take.

And given your existing healthcare/clinical-workflow experience, this also has a natural path beyond the hackathon: **RxNote handles the clinical memory/workflow side, while CarePath could become the patient-facing journey/engagement layer.**

If you want to actually build it for the hackathon, the next artifact I'd create is the **technical implementation spec**: exact Drizzle schema, Next.js routes, AI prompts, RAG pipeline, folder structure, and a **Day 1 → Day 3 build checklist**.

